 "section_summary": "This section contains the concluding portion of the U.S. Embassy in Tokyo's monthly political report on Japan for May 1934, an internal State Department memorandum reviewing the June 1934 report, and the initial portion of the June 1934 monthly report. It documents Japanese foreign policy toward China, diplomatic and border friction with the Soviet Union, trade disputes with the Netherlands East Indies, Great Britain, and Australia, and Brazilian immigration restrictions. It also details domestic political instability surrounding the Kuroda scandal and Saito Cabinet, naval disarmament policy ahead of the 1935 conference, the temporary disappearance of Vice Consul Kuramoto in Nanking, and Japanese alarm over Western arms sales to China.",
