   "start_page": 281,
   "summary": "Drafter E. H. Dooman of the Division of Far Eastern Affairs reviews the Tokyo Embassy's extensive political report for June 1934, identifying significant new material for departmental attention. The memorandum notes Hirota's proposal for bilateral anti-war pacts with the United States and Great Britain, Japanese debates concerning the denunciation of the Washington Naval Treaty, and progress in double-tracking the Trans-Siberian Railway. It especially commends the report's sections analyzing foreign arms sales and aid to China as well as the commercial negotiations between Japan and the Netherlands East Indies in Batavia.",
